      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Most of the clients can take the unity package itself, or get it from the cache at least. I doubt having a password will help with anything other than those clients which clone your avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-20T23:44:19.945Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A lot of times we have to deal with hackers, and what most of the time they do is steal your avatar, a possible solution would be to give the ability to add passwords for private avatars, so if they steal your avatar they'll find themselves with the password, the thing is, if they fail to get the password for an amount of time, OR a certain amount of tries (the latter is the best option in my opinion), the avatar will delete, either from their account or from ID, if that happens it would be fine since the owner will have the original project in unity, so it would just mean to re-upload, this way can be annoying but also let you know when someone stealed your stuff so you're more careful next time",
